{"name":"Autumn Sage","hex":"#aea26e","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"autumn sage","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Salvia greggii, a herbaceous perennial plant native to parts of North America."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/autumn_sage"}],"entries":[{"title":"Salvia greggii","blocks":[{"text":"Salvia greggii, the autumn sage, is a herbaceous perennial plant native to a long, narrow area from southwest Texas, through the Chihuahuan Desert and into the Mexican state of San Luis Potosi, typically growing in rocky soils at elevations from 5,000 to 9,000 ft. It was named and described in 1870 by botanist Asa Gray after Josiah Gregg (1806–1850), a merchant, explorer, naturalist, and author from the American Southwest and Northern Mexico, who found and collected the plant in Texas. It is closely related to, and frequently hybridizes with, Salvia microphylla. Despite the common name \"autumn sage\", it blooms throughout the summer and autumn."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/36/Salvia_greggii_kz2.jpg/330px-Salvia_greggii_kz2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Salvia_greggii","wikidata":"Q891000"},{"title":"Autumn","blocks":[{"text":"Autumn, also known as fall in North American English, is one of the four temperate seasons on Earth. Outside the tropics, autumn marks the transition from summer to winter, beginning in September or March. Autumn is the season when the duration of daytime becomes noticeably shorter and the temperature cools considerably. Day length decreases and night length increases as the season progresses until the winter solstice in December and June. One of its main features in temperate climates is the striking change in colour of the leaves of deciduous trees as they prepare to shed."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d0/D%C3%BClmen%2C_Wildpark_--_2014_--_3808_color_balanced.jpg/330px-D%C3%BClmen%2C_Wildpark_--_2014_--_3808_color_balanced.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Autumn","wikidata":"Q1314"},{"title":"Sage (color)","blocks":[{"text":"Sage is a grey-green resembling that of dried sage leaves. As a quaternary color, it is an equal mix of the tertiary colors citron and slate. The hex RGB color value of the adjacent sage swatch is BCB88A. For decades, some military flight jackets were made in sage green."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b2/Sage_iPhone_17.jpg/330px-Sage_iPhone_17.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sage_(color)","wikidata":"Q7399114"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/46/Salvia_greggii_Coronado_Pink_2.jpg/250px-Salvia_greggii_Coronado_Pink_2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/46/Salvia_greggii_Coronado_Pink_2.jpg/330px-Salvia_greggii_Coronado_Pink_2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/46/Salvia_greggii_Coronado_Pink_2.jpg/250px-Salvia_greggii_Coronado_Pink_2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ASalvia_greggii_Coronado_Pink_2.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d2/Autumn_Sage_%27Teresa%27_%28Salvia_greggii%29.jpg/250px-Autumn_Sage_%27Teresa%27_%28Salvia_greggii%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d2/Autumn_Sage_%27Teresa%27_%28Salvia_greggii%29.jpg/500px-Autumn_Sage_%27Teresa%27_%28Salvia_greggii%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=t